{"id": 17, "ts": 1780644889.6372168, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain inclined toward Candidate\u202fB as the provisional choice, but the lack of any concrete examples of B\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation or adaptability to feedback is a serious gap. While B\u2019s conscientiousness, stress resilience, weather\u2011assessment skill and computer proficiency address reliability, stress\u2011resilience and technical competence, we still have no evidence that B can work effectively with a crew over long\u2011haul flights or adjust to new procedures\u2014both essential for this role. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is noted as 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere, and Candidate\u202fA shows strong leadership and anticipatory skills, yet we also lack technical\u2011competence data for them. To assess whether any of those alternatives might outweigh B\u2019s missing crew\u2011cooperation evidence, I\u2019d like to ask James for any observations on the technical and cognitive competence of Candidates\u202fA,\u202fC, and\u202fD (e.g., system knowledge, navigation skill, problem\u2011solving depth). This will let us compare decision\u2011quality and technical ability across the pool before finalising the recommendation."}
